## Context

On 2026-09-24 the author asked for a strict audit of every harness guard
against the session transcripts, with the stated aim of rationalizing (cutting)
the set. Burden of proof on the guard: it stays only with a quoted firing that
prevented real damage.

Population: 6,417 transcripts (651 main sessions, 5,766 subagent traces,
167 project dirs), 2026-06-01..2026-09-24, count reconciled by an independent
`find | wc -l`. Hook firings were detected by the `PreToolUse:<Tool> hook error:
[<script>]:` prefix on tool_result text only (never Read/cat of source, never
test runs); the detector's positive control fired for every wired hook, and a
missing-script hook error (`check-reviews.sh`, exit 127) is also recorded.

Findings (TP = prevented real damage, FP = blocked a legitimate action):

| Guard | Firings | TP / FP | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| guard-gh-pr-merge (live: block-pr-merge-in-worktree.sh) | 176, all 09-08 | 0 / 176 | never matched any of 893 real `gh pr merge`; live settings points at a file deleted 09-10 |
| guard-pgrep-waiter | 0 | — | never wired live; hazard ran 133× |
| guard-enterworktree-parked-cwd | 32 | 0 | |
| guard-worktree-remove-wip | 17 | 0 | all review scratch / pushed content |
| guard-commit-on-main | 23 | 0 verified / ≥6 | reads session cwd, not the `cd` target; pre-commit covers it |
| guard-destructive-bash | 785 | 1 / most | the one TP is `reset --hard` over a dirty primary (2026-06-18); 657 recursive-force-rm firings 0 TP; one block provoked a worse `git checkout -- file`; it also blocked the heredoc writing this ticket, for quoting its own pattern |
| guard-cd-primary-repo | 93 | 1 / ~20 of 30 | TP recoverable; bypassed via `git -C` |
| guard-worktree-identity | 85 | 4 (one episode) | TPs recoverable; FPs on quoted text, nested repos |
| pretooluse-worktree-path-guard | 62 | 23 / 38 | TPs recoverable; FPs on sibling worktrees |
| inject_rule_on_edit, lint-on-edit, knowledge_hints | — | unmeasurable | ~1.5 M chars injected; no effect shown |
| STALE RULE warning | 343 sessions | — | never resolved |
| bash-env KEYS warning | ~2,400 outputs in 2 days | — | noise, also prefixes hook messages |
| check-settings-drift | 0 visible | — | output discarded: `on-start.sh` redirects to /dev/null before it runs |
| check-pr-open, gaze-gate-lock, check-script-skill-refs | 0 live | — | added the week of 09-17 |

Kept, with their best TP:
- `git reset --hard` block, narrowed to a dirty target tree (2026-06-18, dirty
  settings.json and shell-init.sh in the primary).
- git pre-commit hook: blocked a commit on the primary's main that every
  PreToolUse guard missed (2026-07-13), and a malformed ticket.
- check-cross-pr-ticket-collision (CI): caught tickets 0337/0339 colliding
  with PR #603.

The worktree-trap hooks (cd-primary, identity, path-guard) have only
recoverable TPs, are bypassed immediately, and Claude Code's own worktree
isolation now refuses that class (6,206 refusals in September transcripts).
That overlap is inferred, not tested; the author chose the strict cut.

## Scope (author's decisions, 2026-09-24)

Delete, with their tests, canonical wiring (settings.shared.json,
adapters/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json) and callers:
guard-gh-pr-merge, guard-pgrep-waiter, guard-enterworktree-parked-cwd,
guard-worktree-remove-wip, guard-commit-on-main, guard-cd-primary-repo,
guard-worktree-identity, pretooluse-worktree-path-guard, inject_rule_on_edit,
lint-on-edit, knowledge_hints, warn-stale-rules and the on-start STALE RULE
block, the bash-env KEYS warning line, check-settings-drift,
check-pr-open, gaze-gate-lock, check-script-skill-refs.

Narrow guard-destructive-bash to `git reset --hard` on a dirty tree.

Live `~/.claude/settings.json` is not tracked; it is re-aligned to
settings.shared.json by the author (or a session in the primary) after merge.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Listed scripts, their tests and their wiring are gone; no remaining caller
- [ ] guard-destructive-bash blocks only `git reset --hard` on a dirty tree, with a test
- [ ] Rules, skills and docs no longer instruct agents about deleted guards
- [ ] Full test suite passes
- [ ] Live settings.json re-aligned after merge
